    "description": "Execute one or more filesystem operations against the Hugging Face Hub (ls, cat, stat, find, search, attach) and return their results in a single call. Prefer this for direct file access, directory listing, and Hub discovery tasks. Use hub_repo_search or hub_repo_details instead for structured repo/dataset metadata.\n\nOperations and when to use each:\n- `search`: Discover repos, collections, papers, or docs by keyword\n- `ls`: List a known directory or trending bucket (models/datasets/spaces/papers/trending)\n- `find`: Recursively match files within a known scope using a glob\n- `stat`: Get filesystem metadata when the target type is uncertain; does NOT read file contents\n- `cat`: Read text file contents directly when the URI is known; do not add ls/stat first\n- `attach`: Retrieve a complete JPEG, PNG, or WebP image by URI\n\nSearch scopes: `hf://models|datasets|spaces[/OWNER]`, `hf://collections[/OWNER]`, `hf://papers`, `hf://docs[/...]`. Use `--kind mcp` to filter MCP Spaces. Repeat `--tag` only for space searches.\n\nParameters:\n- operations: Array of `{cmd, args}` objects; multiple operations may be batched in one call. Each `args` is an array of strings forming the command line for that operation.",
    "inputSchema": {
      "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "operations": {
          "items": {
            "additionalProperties": false,
            "properties": {
